      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127414,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127415,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most lesions arise on the trunk, head and neck, and limbs {22892597; 22014540; 28632950; 26268513; 30024070}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127416,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FCTN typically manifests as a solitary, slowly growing, painless plaque-like or nodular skin lesion {22892597; 28632950}. Some agminate cases have been described {31469926; 27296971}, as well as atrophic plaques {28543313} and exophytic tumours {30024070}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127417,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FCTN has a slight female predominance and usually affects young patients (median age: 10&nbsp;years). Congenital cases have been described {30187166; 28067672}, especially on the trunk, as large infiltrated plaques.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127418,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127419,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>KHDRBS1</em>::<em>NTRK3</em> rearrangement has been reported in 1&nbsp;case {30187166}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127420,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127421,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FCTN is a poorly circumscribed lesion localized in the reticular dermis and commonly extending into the superficial subcutis. It is composed of bland spindle-shaped and ovoid cells arranged in a short intersecting fascicular pattern and entrapping appendages that are preserved. Cellularity is variable. Mitotic activity is absent. A storiform pattern may be observed. Epidermal papillomatosis and ectopic dermal adipose tissue are commonly observed {22892597}. Elastic fibres may be decreased in number.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>Expression of CD34 and SMA is described {28632950}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>FCTN overlaps clinically and morphologically with plaque-like CD34-positive dermal fibroma {34449590; 30811625} and dermatomyofibroma {26268513}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127422,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 308,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:45:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
